# Loaded automatically by Expo tooling (`expo export`, `eas build`, `eas update`)
# whenever NODE_ENV=production, which is the default mode for those commands.
# Intentionally versioned: this is a LAN address, not a secret. It takes
# precedence over `.env` (dev-only, gitignored) so production bundles/OTAs
# never depend on shell export order or on what happens to be in the
# developer's local `.env` at publish time.
#
# ALWAYS pass --clear-cache to `eas update` / -c to `expo export` when
# publishing: Metro's transform cache is not keyed by EXPO_PUBLIC_* values,
# so a stale cache entry silently reuses whatever URL was inlined the last
# time api.ts was transformed, regardless of this file's contents.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.15:3001/api/v1
